{"tool_name":"mgwas-explorer","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"mgwas-explorer","home":"https://www.mgwas.ca","summary":"Linking SNPs, Genes, Metabolites, and Diseases for Functional Insights.","addition_date":"2022-09-05T23:16:11.247645Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:41:35.827711Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:mgwas-explorer","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jeff.xia@mcgill.ca","name":"Jianguo Xia","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2040-2624","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Guangyan Zhou"},{"name":"Huiting Ou","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6039-4895"},{"name":"Le Chang","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0966-7923"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Network visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3925"},{"term":"SNP annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3661"}]}],"name":"mGWAS-Explorer","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.3390/metabo12060526","metadata":{"abstract":"Tens of thousands of single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) have been identified to be significantly associated with metabolite abundance in over 65 genome-wide association studies with metabolomics (mGWAS) to date. Obtaining mechanistic or functional insights from these associations for translational applications has become a key research area in the mGWAS community. Here, we introduce mGWAS-Explorer, a user-friendly web-based platform to help connect SNPs, metabolites, genes, and their known disease associations via powerful network visual analytics. The application of the mGWAS-Explorer was demonstrated using a COVID-19 and a type 2 diabetes case studies.","authors":[{"name":"Chang L."},